    "body": "fix on issue/1536-step-tess-hang · PR #1546 · pinned by import_step_guard (a_face_that_never_converges_is_refused_by_name_within_the_budget, a_lowered_cap_refuses_the_same_face_at_once, a_smooth_bspline_face_still_imports_closed_at_its_volume, degenerate_bspline_variants_end_cleanly_and_bounded) and step_guard unit tests · merges when reviewed\n\nRoot cause: truck's `sub_parameter_division` never ends on a B-spline or NURBS surface that is not continuous. One seam stays \"far\" at every depth, and the recursion keeps going even past float resolution. Each face is now metered at our wrapper and refused by name once it passes 25 M evaluations. No thread is used and truck is not patched. This was confirmed on a synthetic discontinuous B-spline face (`testdata/models/bspline_discontinuous.step`), not on `sc_logo.step`, which this worker did not have. Please re-run the repro on a build of the branch. The edge-curve and swept-surface gap is filed as #1545.\n",
